    "created_at": "2016-01-28T06:17:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-28T06:17:26Z",
    "body": "> Should the order be for-in order, or the well-defined order given by [[OwnPropertyKeys]]? (EnumerableOwnNames says for-in order)\n\nCorrect me if I am wrong, but [`for in`](http://www.ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-runtime-semantics-forin-div-ofheadevaluation-tdznames-expr-iterationkind) calls [`[[Enumerate]]`](http://www.ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-ordinary-object-internal-methods-and-internal-slots-enumerate) which calls [`[[OwnPropertyKeys]]`](http://www.ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-ordinary-object-internal-methods-and-internal-slots-ownpropertykeys). They both sort the output keys in the same well-defined way.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
